    "title": "No violation in FPPC complaint against Rivas - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By CHARLES WHISNAND cwhisnand@portervillerecorder.com ,\n1 days ago The California Fair Political Practices Commission has found no violation when it comes to a complaint filed against Porterville City Councilman A.J. Rivas concerning his reporting on residences he owns. Brock Neeley filed the complaint with the FPPC against Rivas for not disclosing any economic interest concerning a residence he... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak 1",
